,"zip":"90-436","country":"Poland","geoPoint":{"lat":51.77058,"lon":19.47395}},{"facility":"Niepubliczny Zaklad Opieki Zdrowotnej Med Laser Borzecki Spolka Jawna","city":"Lublin","zip":"20-406","country":"Poland","geoPoint":{"lat":51.25058,"lon":22.57009}},{"facility":"Tomasz Blicharski Lubelskie Centrum Diagnostyczne","city":"Świdnik","zip":"21-040","country":"Poland","geoPoint":{"lat":51.21898,"lon":22.69621}},{"facility":"Centrum Medyczne Pratia Warszawa","city":"Warsaw","zip":"01-868","country":"Poland","geoPoint":{"lat":52.22977,"lon":21.01178}},{"facility":"Medicus Sp z o o","city":"Wroclaw","zip":"50-224","country":"Poland","geoPoint":{"lat":51.10286,"lon":17.03006}},{"facility":"DermMedica Spzoo","city":"Wroclaw","zip":"51-318","country":"Poland","geoPoint":{"lat":51.10286,"lon":17.03006}},{"facility":"Hallym University Kangnam Sacred Heart Hospital","city":"Seoul","zip":"07441","country":"South Korea","geoPoint":{"lat":37.566,"lon":126.9784}},{"facility":"Hospital Universitario Virgen Macarena","city":"Seville","state":"AndalucÃ-a","zip":"41009","country":"Spain","geoPoint":{"lat":37.38283,"lon":-5.97317}},{"facility":"Hospital Universitari Germans Trias i Pujol","city":"Badalona","state":"CataluÃ±a","zip":"08916","country":"Spain","geoPoint":{"lat":41.45004,"lon":2.24741}},{"facility":"Hospital del Mar","city":"Barcelona","state":"CataluÃ±a","zip":"08003","country":"Spain","geoPoint":{"lat":41.38879,"lon":2.15899}},{"facility":"Hospital de la Santa Creu i Sant Pau","city":"Barcelona","state":"CataluÃ±a","zip":"08041","country":"Spain","geoPoint":{"lat":41.38879,"lon":2.15899}},{"facility":"Hospital General Universitario de Alicante","city":"Alicante","state":"Valencia","zip":"03010","country":"Spain","geoPoint":{"lat":38.34517,"lon":-0.48149}},{"facility":"Hospital Universitario de La Princesa","city":"Madrid","zip":"28006","country":"Spain","geoPoint":{"lat":40.4165,"lon":-3.70256}},{"facility":"Centre Hospitalier Universitaire Vaudois","city":"Lausanne","zip":"1011","country":"Switzerland","geoPoint":{"lat":46.516,"lon":6.63282}},{"facility":"Chernivtsi Regional Skin and Venereal Dispensary","city":"Chernivtsi","zip":"58002","country":"Ukraine","geoPoint":{"lat":48.29045,"lon":25.93241}},{"facility":"Regional Skin and Venereal Dispensary","city":"Dnipro","zip":"49074","country":"Ukraine","geoPoint":{"lat":48.46664,"lon":35.04066}},{"facility":"Ivano-Frankivsk Regional Skin and Venereal Dispensary","city":"Ivano-Frankivsk","zip":"76018","country":"Ukraine","geoPoint":{"lat":48.92312,"lon":24.71248}},{"facility":"Medical clinic Blagomed","city":"Kyiv","zip":"02000","country":"Ukraine","geoPoint":{"lat":50.45466,"lon":30.5238}},{"facility":"Asclepius","city":"Uzhhorod","zip":"88000","country":"Ukraine","geoPoint":{"lat":48.6242,"lon":22.2947}},{"facility":"Military Hospital, Military Unit A3309 of the Military Medical Clinical Center","city":"Zaporizhzhya","zip":"69000","country":"Ukraine","geoPoint":{"lat":47.85167,"lon":35.11714}},{"facility":"Ninewells Hospital","city":"Dundee","zip":"DD1 9SY","country":"United Kingdom","geoPoint":{"lat":56.46913,"lon":-2.97489}},{"facility":"Whipps Cross University Hospital","city":"London","zip":"E11 1NR","country":"United Kingdom","geoPoint":{"lat":51.50853,"lon":-0.12574}},{"facility":"Southampton General Hospital","city":"Southampton","zip":"SO16 6YD","country":"United Kingdom","geoPoint":{"lat":50.90395,"lon":-1.40428}}]},"referencesModule":{"seeAlsoLinks":[{"label":"AmgenTrials clinical trials website","url":"http://www.amgentrials.com"}]},"ipdSharingStatementModule":{"ipdSharing":"YES","description":"De-identified individual patient data for variables necessary to address the specific research question in an approved data sharing request","infoTypes":["STUDY_PROTOCOL","SAP","ICF","CSR"],"timeFrame":"Data sharing requests relating to this study will be considered beginning 18 months after the study has ended and either 1) the product and indication have been granted marketing authorization in both the US and Europe or 2) clinical development for the product and/or indication discontinues and the data will not be submitted to regulatory authorities. There is no end date for eligibility to submit a data sharing request for this study.","accessCriteria":"Qualified researchers may submit a request containing the research objectives, the Amgen product(s) and Amgen study/studies in scope, endpoints/outcomes of interest, statistical analysis plan, data requirements, publication plan, and qualifications of the researcher(s). In general, Amgen does not grant external requests for individual patient data for the purpose of re-evaluating safety and efficacy issues already addressed in the product labelling. Requests are reviewed by a committee of internal advisors. If not approved, a Data Sharing Independent Review Panel will arbitrate and make the final decision. Upon approval, information necessary to address the research question will be provided under the terms of a data sharing agreement. This may include anonymized individual patient data and/or available supporting documents, containing fragments of analysis code where provided in analysis specifications. Further details are available at the URL below.","url":"https://www.amgen.com/datasharing"}},"resultsSection":{"participantFlowModule":{"preAssignmentDetails":"Enrollment of Part A of this study was completed as of 27 July 2020. The study was terminated prior to the enrollment of any participants into Part B.","recruitmentDetails":"Participants were enrolled in 78 centers in 14 countries including Australia, Canada, Czech Republic, Estonia, Germany, Hungary, Japan, Latvia, Poland, Republic of Korea, Spain, Ukraine, the United Kingdom, and the United States.","groups":[{"id":"FG000","title":"Part A: Placebo","description":"Matching placebo administered via subcutaneous (SC) injection once every 2 weeks (Q2W) for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in Eczema Area and Severity Index \\[EASI\\] compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"FG001","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 210 mg Q4W","description":"Tezepelumab 210 mg administered via SC injection once every 4 weeks (Q4W) from Week 4 for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nAll participants randomized to tezepelumab received 420 mg SC injection as their first dose. Participants then received a placebo at Week 2 and every other week to maintain blinding.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"FG002","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 280 mg Q2W","description":"Tezepelumab 280 mg administered via SC injection Q2W from Week 2 for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nAll participants randomized to tezepelumab received 420 mg SC injection as their first dose. Participants then received their randomized dose of 280 mg Q2W from Week 2.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"FG003","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 420 mg Q2W","description":"Tezepelumab 420 mg administered via SC injection Q2W for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 stayed to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"FG004","title":"Part B: Placebo and Topical Corticosteroids Regimen","description":"Matching placebo was planned to be administered via SC injection Q2W with topical corticosteroids (TCS) for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nThe study was terminated prior to the start of Part 2 and no participants were enrolled."},{"id":"FG005","title":"Part B: Tezepelumab 420 mg Q2W and Topical Corticosteroids Regimen","description":"Tezepelumab 420 mg was planned to be administered via SC injection Q2W with TCS for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nThe study was terminated prior to the start of Part 2 and no participants were enrolled."}],"periods":[{"title":"Overall Study","milestones":[{"type":"STARTED","achievements":[{"groupId":"FG000","numSubjects":"63"},{"groupId":"FG001","numSubjects":"62"},{"groupId":"FG002","numSubjects":"63"},{"groupId":"FG003","numSubjects":"63"},{"groupId":"FG004","numSubjects":"0"},{"groupId":"FG005","numSubjects":"0"}]},{"type":"Participants Who Received Investigational Product","achievements":[{"groupId":"FG000","numSubjects":"63"},{"groupId":"FG001","numSubjects":"61"},{"groupId":"FG002","numSubjects":"63"},{"groupId":"FG003","numSubjects":"63"},{"groupId":"FG004","numSubjects":"0"},{"groupId":"FG005","numSubjects":"0"}]},{"type":"EASI 50 Non-responder at Week 16","achievements":[{"groupId":"FG000","numSubjects":"40"},{"groupId":"FG001","numSubjects":"26"},{"groupId":"FG002","numSubjects":"30"},{"groupId":"FG003","numSubjects":"38"},{"groupId":"FG004","numSubjects":"0"},{"groupId":"FG005","numSubjects":"0"}]},{"type":"Switched to Tezepelumab 420 mg Q2W After Week 16","achievements":[{"groupId":"FG000","numSubjects":"39"},{"groupId":"FG001","numSubjects":"24"},{"groupId":"FG002","numSubjects":"30"},{"groupId":"FG003","numSubjects":"38"},{"groupId":"FG004","numSubjects":"0"},{"groupId":"FG005","numSubjects":"0"}]},{"type":"COMPLETED","achievements":[{"groupId":"FG000","numSubjects":"12"},{"groupId":"FG001","numSubjects":"18"},{"groupId":"FG002","numSubjects":"15"},{"groupId":"FG003","numSubjects":"16"},{"groupId":"FG004","numSubjects":"0"},{"groupId":"FG005","numSubjects":"0"}]},{"type":"NOT COMPLETED","achievements":[{"groupId":"FG000","numSubjects":"51"},{"groupId":"FG001","numSubjects":"44"},{"groupId":"FG002","numSubjects":"48"},{"groupId":"FG003","numSubjects":"47"},{"groupId":"FG004","numSubjects":"0"},{"groupId":"FG005","numSubjects":"0"}]}],"dropWithdraws":[{"type":"Decision by sponsor","reasons":[{"groupId":"FG000","numSubjects":"24"},{"groupId":"FG001","numSubjects":"18"},{"groupId":"FG002","numSubjects":"20"},{"groupId":"FG003","numSubjects":"20"},{"groupId":"FG004","numSubjects":"0"},{"groupId":"FG005","numSubjects":"0"}]},{"type":"Withdrawal by Subject","reasons":[{"groupId":"FG000","numSubjects":"26"},{"groupId":"FG001","numSubjects":"22"},{"groupId":"FG002","numSubjects":"27"},{"groupId":"FG003","numSubjects":"26"},{"groupId":"FG004","numSubjects":"0"},{"groupId":"FG005","numSubjects":"0"}]},{"type":"Lost to Follow-up","reasons":[{"groupId":"FG000","numSubjects":"1"},{"groupId":"FG001","numSubjects":"4"},{"groupId":"FG002","numSubjects":"1"},{"groupId":"FG003","numSubjects":"1"},{"groupId":"FG004","numSubjects":"0"},{"groupId":"FG005","numSubjects":"0"}]}]}]},"baselineCharacteristicsModule":{"populationDescription":"Full analysis set (FAS): All randomized participants in Part A.","groups":[{"id":"BG000","title":"Part A: Placebo","description":"Matching placebo administered via subcutaneous (SC) injection once every 2 weeks (Q2W) for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in Eczema Area and Severity Index \\[EASI\\] compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"BG001","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 210 mg Q4W","description":"Tezepelumab 210 mg administered via SC injection once every 4 weeks (Q4W) from Week 4 for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nAll participants randomized to tezepelumab received 420 mg SC injection as their first dose. Participants then received a placebo at Week 2 and every other week to maintain blinding.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"BG002","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 280 mg Q2W","description":"Tezepelumab 280 mg administered via SC injection Q2W from Week 2 for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nAll participants randomized to tezepelumab received 420 mg SC injection as their first dose. Participants then received their randomized dose of 280 mg Q2W from Week 2.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"BG003","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 420 mg Q2W","description":"Tezepelumab 420 mg administered via SC injection Q2W for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 stayed to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"BG004","title":"Total","description":"Total of all reporting groups"}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"BG000","value":"63"},{"groupId":"BG001","value":"62"},{"groupId":"BG002","value":"63"},{"groupId":"BG003","value":"63"},{"groupId":"BG004","value":"251"}]}],"measures":[{"title":"Age, Continuous","paramType":"MEAN","dispersionType":"STANDARD_DEVIATION","unitOfMeasure":"Years","classes":[{"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"BG000","value":"35.7","spread":"13.4"},{"groupId":"BG001","value":"38.5","spread":"15.0"},{"groupId":"BG002","value":"36.9","spread":"13.4"},{"groupId":"BG003","value":"40.7","spread":"14.3"},{"groupId":"BG004","value":"37.9","spread":"14.1"}]}]}]},{"title":"Sex: Female, Male","paramType":"COUNT_OF_PARTICIPANTS","unitOfMeasure":"Participants","classes":[{"categories":[{"title":"Female","measurements":[{"groupId":"BG000","value":"27"},{"groupId":"BG001","value":"32"},{"groupId":"BG002","value":"23"},{"groupId":"BG003","value":"27"},{"groupId":"BG004","value":"109"}]},{"title":"Male","measurements":[{"groupId":"BG000","value":"36"},{"groupId":"BG001","value":"30"},{"groupId":"BG002","value":"40"},{"groupId":"BG003","value":"36"},{"groupId":"BG004","value":"142"}]}]}]},{"title":"Ethnicity (NIH/OMB)","paramType":"COUNT_OF_PARTICIPANTS","unitOfMeasure":"Participants","classes":[{"categories":[{"title":"Hispanic or Latino","measurements":[{"groupId":"BG000","value":"6"},{"groupId":"BG001","value":"4"},{"groupId":"BG002","value":"1"},{"groupId":"BG003","value":"4"},{"groupId":"BG004","value":"15"}]},{"title":"Not Hispanic or Latino","measurements":[{"groupId":"BG000","value":"57"},{"groupId":"BG001","value":"58"},{"groupId":"BG002","value":"62"},{"groupId":"BG003","value":"59"},{"groupId":"BG004","value":"236"}]},{"title":"Unknown or Not Reported","measurements":[{"groupId":"BG000","value":"0"},{"groupId":"BG001","value":"0"},{"groupId":"BG002","value":"0"},{"groupId":"BG003","value":"0"},{"groupId":"BG004","value":"0"}]}]}]},{"title":"Race/Ethnicity, Customized","paramType":"COUNT_OF_PARTICIPANTS","unitOfMeasure":"Participants","classes":[{"categories":[{"title":"American Indian or Alaska Native","measurements":[{"groupId":"BG000","value":"0"},{"groupId":"BG001","value":"1"},{"groupId":"BG002","value":"0"},{"groupId":"BG003","value":"0"},{"groupId":"BG004","value":"1"}]},{"title":"Asian","measurements":[{"groupId":"BG000","value":"21"},{"groupId":"BG001","value":"16"},{"groupId":"BG002","value":"16"},{"groupId":"BG003","value":"13"},{"groupId":"BG004","value":"66"}]},{"title":"Black or African-American","measurements":[{"groupId":"BG000","value":"1"},{"groupId":"BG001","value":"3"},{"groupId":"BG002","value":"1"},{"groupId":"BG003","value":"3"},{"groupId":"BG004","value":"8"}]},{"title":"Native Hawaiian or Other Pacific Islander","measurements":[{"groupId":"BG000","value":"0"},{"groupId":"BG001","value":"0"},{"groupId":"BG002","value":"0"},{"groupId":"BG003","value":"0"},{"groupId":"BG004","value":"0"}]},{"title":"White","measurements":[{"groupId":"BG000","value":"41"},{"groupId":"BG001","value":"42"},{"groupId":"BG002","value":"45"},{"groupId":"BG003","value":"47"},{"groupId":"BG004","value":"175"}]},{"title":"Unknown","measurements":[{"groupId":"BG000","value":"0"},{"groupId":"BG001","value":"0"},{"groupId":"BG002","value":"0"},{"groupId":"BG003","value":"0"},{"groupId":"BG004","value":"0"}]},{"title":"Other","measurements":[{"groupId":"BG000","value":"0"},{"groupId":"BG001","value":"0"},{"groupId":"BG002","value":"1"},{"groupId":"BG003","value":"0"},{"groupId":"BG004","value":"1"}]}]}]},{"title":"Investigator's Global Assessment Score","description":"The IGA allows investigators to assess overall disease severity at 1 given time point and consists of a 6-point severity scale from clear to severe disease\n\n* 0 = clear\n* 1 = almost clear\n* 2 = mild disease\n* 3 = moderate disease\n* 4 = severe disease\n* 5 = very severe disease The IGA uses clinical characteristics of erythema, infiltration, papulation, oozing \\& crusting as guidelines for the overall severity assessment (Breuer et al 2004).","paramType":"COUNT_OF_PARTICIPANTS","unitOfMeasure":"Participants","classes":[{"categories":[{"title":"IGA Score of 3","measurements":[{"groupId":"BG000","value":"26"},{"groupId":"BG001","value":"37"},{"groupId":"BG002","value":"26"},{"groupId":"BG003","value":"37"},{"groupId":"BG004","value":"126"}]},{"title":"IGA Score of 4","measurements":[{"groupId":"BG000","value":"32"},{"groupId":"BG001","value":"17"},{"groupId":"BG002","value":"30"},{"groupId":"BG003","value":"18"},{"groupId":"BG004","value":"97"}]},{"title":"IGA Score of 5","measurements":[{"groupId":"BG000","value":"5"},{"groupId":"BG001","value":"8"},{"groupId":"BG002","value":"7"},{"groupId":"BG003","value":"8"},{"groupId":"BG004","value":"28"}]}]}]},{"title":"Eczema Area and Severity Index (EASI)","description":"The EASI was designed by modifying the Psoriasis Area and Severity Index (Schmitt et al, 2007). The EASI evaluates 4 natural anatomical regions for severity and extent of key disease signs and focuses on key acute and chronic signs of inflammation (ie, erythema, induration/papulation, excoriation, and lichenification).\n\nThe lowest possible total score is 0 and the highest possible total score is 72, with higher scores indicating greater severity of eczema.","paramType":"MEAN","dispersionType":"STANDARD_DEVIATION","unitOfMeasure":"Score on a scale","classes":[{"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"BG000","value":"32.0","spread":"11.1"},{"groupId":"BG001","value":"28.4","spread":"13.2"},{"groupId":"BG002","value":"30.3","spread":"10.7"},{"groupId":"BG003","value":"28.6","spread":"12.4"},{"groupId":"BG004","value":"29.8","spread":"11.9"}]}]}]}]},"outcomeMeasuresModule":{"outcomeMeasures":[{"type":"PRIMARY","title":"Number of Participants With Investigator's Global Assessment (IGA) Score of 0 (Clear) or 1 (Almost Clear) (IGA 0/1) at Week 16","description":"The IGA allows investigators to assess overall disease severity at 1 given time point and consists of a 6-point severity scale from clear to severe disease\n\n* 0 = clear\n* 1 = almost clear\n* 2 = mild disease\n* 3 = moderate disease\n* 4 = severe disease\n* 5 = very severe disease\n\nThe IGA uses clinical characteristics of erythema, infiltration, papulation, oozing, and crusting as guidelines for the overall severity assessment (Breuer et al, 2004).\n\nParticipants who took rescue medication between Day 29 to Week 16 were considered non-responders.","populationDescription":"FAS: All randomized participants.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"COUNT_OF_PARTICIPANTS","unitOfMeasure":"Participants","timeFrame":"Week 16","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Part A: Placebo","description":"Matching placebo administered via subcutaneous (SC) injection once every 2 weeks (Q2W) for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in Eczema Area and Severity Index \\[EASI\\] compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 210 mg Q4W","description":"Tezepelumab 210 mg administered via SC injection once every 4 weeks (Q4W) from Week 4 for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nAll participants randomized to tezepelumab received 420 mg SC injection as their first dose. Participants then received a placebo at Week 2 and every other week to maintain blinding.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG002","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 280 mg Q2W","description":"Tezepelumab 280 mg administered via SC injection Q2W from Week 2 for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nAll participants randomized to tezepelumab received 420 mg SC injection as their first dose. Participants then received their randomized dose of 280 mg Q2W from Week 2.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG003","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 420 mg Q2W","description":"Tezepelumab 420 mg administered via SC injection Q2W for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 stayed to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"63"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"62"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"63"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"63"}]}],"classes":[{"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"2"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"4"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"2"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"5"}]}]}],"analyses":[{"groupIds":["OG000","OG001"],"nonInferiorityType":"SUPERIORITY","pValue":"0.56","pValueComment":"Nominal p-value","statisticalMethod":"Regression, Logistic","paramType":"Odds Ratio (OR)","paramValue":"1.686","ciPctValue":"95","ciNumSides":"TWO_SIDED","ciLowerLimit":"0.290","ciUpperLimit":"9.809"},{"groupIds":["OG000","OG002"],"nonInferiorityType":"SUPERIORITY","pValue":"0.99","pValueComment":"Nominal p-value","statisticalMethod":"Regression, Logistic","paramType":"Odds Ratio (OR)","paramValue":"1.011","ciPctValue":"95","ciNumSides":"TWO_SIDED","ciLowerLimit":"0.135","ciUpperLimit":"7.551"},{"groupIds":["OG000","OG003"],"nonInferiorityType":"SUPERIORITY","pValue":"0.38","pValueComment":"Nominal p-value","statisticalMethod":"Regression, Logistic","paramType":"Odds Ratio (OR)","paramValue":"2.146","ciPctValue":"95","ciNumSides":"TWO_SIDED","ciLowerLimit":"0.390","ciUpperLimit":"11.800"}]},{"type":"PRIMARY","title":"Number of Participants Who Experienced a 75% Reduction From Baseline in Eczema Area and Severity Index (EASI 75) at Week 16","description":"The EASI evaluates 4 natural anatomical regions for severity and extent of key disease signs and focuses on key acute and chronic signs of inflammation (ie, erythema, induration/papulation, excoriation, and lichenification).\n\nA reduction in the EASI score indicates an improvement in severity. Participants who took rescue medication between Day 29 to Week 16 were considered non-responders.","populationDescription":"FAS: All randomized participants.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"COUNT_OF_PARTICIPANTS","unitOfMeasure":"Participants","timeFrame":"Baseline and Week 16","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Part A: Placebo","description":"Matching placebo administered via subcutaneous (SC) injection once every 2 weeks (Q2W) for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in Eczema Area and Severity Index \\[EASI\\] compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 210 mg Q4W","description":"Tezepelumab 210 mg administered via SC injection once every 4 weeks (Q4W) from Week 4 for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nAll participants randomized to tezepelumab received 420 mg SC injection as their first dose. Participants then received a placebo at Week 2 and every other week to maintain blinding.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG002","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 280 mg Q2W","description":"Tezepelumab 280 mg administered via SC injection Q2W from Week 2 for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nAll participants randomized to tezepelumab received 420 mg SC injection as their first dose. Participants then received their randomized dose of 280 mg Q2W from Week 2.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG003","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 420 mg Q2W","description":"Tezepelumab 420 mg administered via SC injection Q2W for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 stayed to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"63"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"62"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"63"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"63"}]}],"classes":[{"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"8"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"9"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"10"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"7"}]}]}],"analyses":[{"groupIds":["OG000","OG001"],"nonInferiorityType":"SUPERIORITY","pValue":"0.97","pValueComment":"Nominal p-value","statisticalMethod":"Regression, Logistic","paramType":"Odds Ratio (OR)","paramValue":"0.982","ciPctValue":"95","ciNumSides":"TWO_SIDED","ciLowerLimit":"0.344","ciUpperLimit":"2.803"},{"groupIds":["OG000","OG002"],"nonInferiorityType":"SUPERIORITY","pValue":"0.70","pValueComment":"Nominal p-value","statisticalMethod":"Regression, Logistic","paramType":"Odds Ratio (OR)","paramValue":"1.217","ciPctValue":"95","ciNumSides":"TWO_SIDED","ciLowerLimit":"0.441","ciUpperLimit":"3.356"},{"groupIds":["OG000","OG003"],"nonInferiorityType":"SUPERIORITY","pValue":"0.58","pValueComment":"Nominal p-value","statisticalMethod":"Regression, Logistic","paramType":"Odds Ratio (OR)","paramValue":"0.730","ciPctValue":"95","ciNumSides":"TWO_SIDED","ciLowerLimit":"0.243","ciUpperLimit":"2.197"}]},{"type":"SECONDARY","title":"Number of Participants Who Experienced a 50% or 90% Reduction From Baseline in Eczema Area and Severity Index (EASI 50/90) at Week 16","description":"The EASI evaluates 4 natural anatomical regions for severity and extent of key disease signs and focuses on key acute and chronic signs of inflammation (ie, erythema, induration/papulation, excoriation, and lichenification).\n\nA reduction in the EASI score indicates an improvement in severity. Participants who took rescue medication between Day 29 to Week 16 were considered non-responders.","populationDescription":"FAS: All randomized participants.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"COUNT_OF_PARTICIPANTS","unitOfMeasure":"Participants","timeFrame":"Baseline and Week 16","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Part A: Placebo","description":"Matching placebo administered via subcutaneous (SC) injection once every 2 weeks (Q2W) for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in Eczema Area and Severity Index \\[EASI\\] compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 210 mg Q4W","description":"Tezepelumab 210 mg administered via SC injection once every 4 weeks (Q4W) from Week 4 for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nAll participants randomized to tezepelumab received 420 mg SC injection as their first dose. Participants then received a placebo at Week 2 and every other week to maintain blinding.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG002","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 280 mg Q2W","description":"Tezepelumab 280 mg administered via SC injection Q2W from Week 2 for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nAll participants randomized to tezepelumab received 420 mg SC injection as their first dose. Participants then received their randomized dose of 280 mg Q2W from Week 2.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG003","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 420 mg Q2W","description":"Tezepelumab 420 mg administered via SC injection Q2W for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 stayed to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"56"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"58"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"58"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"56"}]}],"classes":[{"title":"EASI 50","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"11"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"21"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"18"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"11"}]}]},{"title":"EASI 90","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"3"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"3"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"3"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"3"}]}]}]},{"type":"SECONDARY","title":"Time to Achievement of 50%, 75% or 90% Reduction From Day 1 in Eczema Area and Severity Index (EASI 50/75/90)","populationDescription":"FAS: All randomized participants.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"MEDIAN","dispersionType":"Full Range","unitOfMeasure":"Weeks","timeFrame":"Day 1 up to End of Study Visit (Week 70)","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Part A: Placebo","description":"Matching placebo administered via subcutaneous (SC) injection once every 2 weeks (Q2W) for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in Eczema Area and Severity Index \\[EASI\\] compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 210 mg Q4W","description":"Tezepelumab 210 mg administered via SC injection once every 4 weeks (Q4W) from Week 4 for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nAll participants randomized to tezepelumab received 420 mg SC injection as their first dose. Participants then received a placebo at Week 2 and every other week to maintain blinding.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG002","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 280 mg Q2W","description":"Tezepelumab 280 mg administered via SC injection Q2W from Week 2 for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nAll participants randomized to tezepelumab received 420 mg SC injection as their first dose. Participants then received their randomized dose of 280 mg Q2W from Week 2.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG003","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 420 mg Q2W","description":"Tezepelumab 420 mg administered via SC injection Q2W for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 stayed to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"63"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"62"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"63"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"63"}]}],"classes":[{"title":"Time to EASI 50","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"6.143","lowerLimit":"4.14","upperLimit":"19.57"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"8.143","lowerLimit":"3.86","upperLimit":"16.14"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"6.286","lowerLimit":"3.86","upperLimit":"22.14"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"5.857","lowerLimit":"3.86","upperLimit":"16.14"}]}]},{"title":"Time to EASI 75","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"6.143","lowerLimit":"4.14","upperLimit":"19.57"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"6.286","lowerLimit":"4.00","upperLimit":"16.43"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"6.714","lowerLimit":"4.14","upperLimit":"22.14"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"6.429","lowerLimit":"4.14","upperLimit":"16.14"}]}]},{"title":"Time to EASI 90","categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"8.286","lowerLimit":"4.43","upperLimit":"19.57"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"10.929","lowerLimit":"4.00","upperLimit":"16.14"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"10.071","lowerLimit":"6.14","upperLimit":"16.14"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"7.286","lowerLimit":"4.14","upperLimit":"16.29"}]}]}]},{"type":"SECONDARY","title":"Change From Baseline in Scoring of Atopic Dermatitis (SCORAD) at Week 16","description":"The SCORAD is a clinical tool for assessing the severity (ie, extent, intensity) of atopic dermatitis (AD). The tool evaluates the extent and intensity of the AD lesions, along with subjective symptoms (Kunz et al, 1997). The total score ranges from 0 to 103, with higher values indicating more severe disease. A negative change from baseline indicates an improvement in severity of disease.","populationDescription":"FAS: All randomized participants.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"LEAST_SQUARES_MEAN","dispersionType":"Standard Error","unitOfMeasure":"Score on a scale","timeFrame":"Baseline and Week 16","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Part A: Placebo","description":"Matching placebo administered via subcutaneous (SC) injection once every 2 weeks (Q2W) for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in Eczema Area and Severity Index \\[EASI\\] compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 210 mg Q4W","description":"Tezepelumab 210 mg administered via SC injection once every 4 weeks (Q4W) from Week 4 for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nAll participants randomized to tezepelumab received 420 mg SC injection as their first dose. Participants then received a placebo at Week 2 and every other week to maintain blinding.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG002","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 280 mg Q2W","description":"Tezepelumab 280 mg administered via SC injection Q2W from Week 2 for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nAll participants randomized to tezepelumab received 420 mg SC injection as their first dose. Participants then received their randomized dose of 280 mg Q2W from Week 2.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG003","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 420 mg Q2W","description":"Tezepelumab 420 mg administered via SC injection Q2W for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 stayed to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"63"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"62"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"63"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"63"}]}],"classes":[{"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"-8.00","spread":"2.55"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"-16.75","spread":"2.40"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"-11.87","spread":"2.49"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"-9.32","spread":"2.48"}]}]}]},{"type":"SECONDARY","title":"Change From Baseline in Pruritus Numeric Rating Scale (NRS) at Week 16","description":"Pruritus was assessed using an NRS (0-10) with 0 = no itch and 10 = worst imaginable itch. A negative change from baseline indicates an improvement in symptoms.","populationDescription":"FAS: All randomized participants.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"LEAST_SQUARES_MEAN","dispersionType":"Standard Error","unitOfMeasure":"Score on a scale","timeFrame":"Baseline and Week 16","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Part A: Placebo","description":"Matching placebo administered via subcutaneous (SC) injection once every 2 weeks (Q2W) for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in Eczema Area and Severity Index \\[EASI\\] compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 210 mg Q4W","description":"Tezepelumab 210 mg administered via SC injection once every 4 weeks (Q4W) from Week 4 for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nAll participants randomized to tezepelumab received 420 mg SC injection as their first dose. Participants then received a placebo at Week 2 and every other week to maintain blinding.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG002","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 280 mg Q2W","description":"Tezepelumab 280 mg administered via SC injection Q2W from Week 2 for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nAll participants randomized to tezepelumab received 420 mg SC injection as their first dose. Participants then received their randomized dose of 280 mg Q2W from Week 2.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG003","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 420 mg Q2W","description":"Tezepelumab 420 mg administered via SC injection Q2W for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 stayed to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"63"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"62"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"63"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"63"}]}],"classes":[{"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"-0.71","spread":"0.30"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"-1.40","spread":"0.27"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"-0.94","spread":"0.28"},{"groupId":"OG003","value":"-0.38","spread":"0.28"}]}]}]},{"type":"SECONDARY","title":"Serum Trough Concentrations of Tezepelumab After Q2W or Q4W Administration","description":"Switchers were included up to Week 16 and were then excluded from the analysis after switching. All Tezepelumab participants received 420 mg of Tezepelumab on Day 1.","populationDescription":"All randomized participants who received at least 1 dose of investigational product with analyzable samples at each time point. Participants were analyzed according to the highest dose of actual treatment received after initial first dose or only dose received. Switchers were included up to Week 16 and were then excluded from the analysis after switching at Week 16.","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"MEAN","dispersionType":"Standard Deviation","unitOfMeasure":"µg/mL","timeFrame":"Pre-dose on Day 1, Week 2, 4, 12, 16, 24, 32, 40, 48, 50, 52, 58 and 70","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 210 mg Q4W","description":"Tezepelumab 210 mg administered via SC injection once every 4 weeks (Q4W) from Week 4 for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nAll participants randomized to tezepelumab received 420 mg SC injection as their first dose. Participants then received a placebo at Week 2 and every other week to maintain blinding.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG001","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 280 mg Q2W","description":"Tezepelumab 280 mg administered via SC injection Q2W from Week 2 for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nAll participants randomized to tezepelumab received 420 mg SC injection as their first dose. Participants then received their randomized dose of 280 mg Q2W from Week 2.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 switched to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."},{"id":"OG002","title":"Part A: Tezepelumab 420 mg Q2W","description":"Tezepelumab 420 mg administered via SC injection Q2W for a maximum of 52 weeks.\n\nParticipants defined as non-responders (those who did not achieve at least 50% improvement in EASI compared to baseline) at Week 16 stayed to receive tezepelumab 420 mg SC injection Q2W for the remainder of the study."}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"58"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"58"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"66"}]}],"classes":[{"title":"Day 1","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"58"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"58"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"66"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"0.00031","spread":"0.00236"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"0.00","spread":"0.00"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"0.00","spread":"0.00"}]}]},{"title":"Week 2","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"51"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"49"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"60"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"34.9","spread":"10.9"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"36.3","spread":"12.9"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"34.8","spread":"12.9"}]}]},{"title":"Week 4","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"56"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"48"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"53"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"23.4","spread":"9.03"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"48.8","spread":"16.0"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"58.9","spread":"21.4"}]}]},{"title":"Week 12","denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"49"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"48"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"47"}]}],"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"21.7","spread":"8.47"},{"groupId":"OG001","value":"66.7","spread":"22.9"},{"groupId":"OG002","value":"97.0","spread":"35.0"}]}]},{"title":"Week 16","denoms":[{"units":"Part